The changes pass the existing tests and the new cancellation/cap tests. Demand now blocks new async dispatch while it prepares and completes its fill; already-running async chunks finish normally. Cancellation removes queued work for the arriving layer and older layers, and clears leftover queues when layer numbering restarts for a new microbatch. Next I’ll generate both patches and verify fresh application, header equality, compilation, and the eight-run spec.
